# cairo -- the 2D drawing model GTK's older widgets and every PDF or PNG export
# path still go through. GTK 4 renders through its own GPU renderer, but cairo
# is not optional: pango's font backends, gdk-pixbuf's scaling and a long tail
# of widgets draw with it.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://www.cairographics.org/releases/cairo-1.18.4.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=445ed8208a6e4823de1226a74ca319d3600e83f6369f99b14265006599c32ccb
SRC_DIR=cairo-1.18.4

# -Dxlib=enabled, AND THE REASON IT WAS DISABLED IS WORTH KEEPING RATHER THAN
# OVERWRITING, because it was not wrong -- it was about a different thing.
#
# It read: "xlib and xcb are disabled to match mesa, which is built without
# GLX: there is no X server here, so an X backend would be an interface with
# nothing behind it."
#
# The GLX half of that is exactly right and still is. GLX is OpenGL delivered
# through an X server, and this tree has no X server, so mesa is built without
# it. What the clause then did was carry that conclusion across to cairo's
# xlib surface, which is a different thing: cairo-xlib is drawing to an X
# DRAWABLE, which is what any X CLIENT does -- and X clients do exist here,
# because Xwayland is now packaged and is exactly the server they talk to.
#
# THE CONSUMER THAT SURFACED IT is mutter-x11-frames, the GTK 4 helper that
# draws server-side decorations for X11 windows under Xwayland. mutter builds
# it unconditionally whenever X11 client support is on -- there is no option to
# drop it -- and it is itself an X client, so it needs gtk4's X11 backend,
# which needs cairo-xlib. Nothing was wrong with this recipe until a package
# that did not exist when it was written asked for the thing it had turned off.
#
# ONLY xlib. -Dxcb and -Dxlib-xcb stay disabled: gtk4's meson.build resolves
# exactly one cairo backend for its X11 build, 'cairo-xlib' (the cairo_backends
# loop, 491-503), and nothing else in the tree asks for the xcb surfaces.
# Enabling them "to match" would acquire libxcb surface code no consumer wants,
# which is the habit this tree spends most of its comments avoiding.
#
# What xlib costs: x11, xext and xrender, all three already packaged in
# GRAPHICS_PKGS, which precedes this group. No new package anywhere.
#
# tee is a debugging backend.
MESON_ARGS="-Dxlib=enabled -Dxcb=disabled -Dxlib-xcb=disabled -Dtee=disabled \
-Dglib=enabled -Dfreetype=enabled -Dfontconfig=enabled -Dpng=enabled \
-Dtests=disabled -Dgtk_doc=false -Dspectre=disabled -Dsymbol-lookup=disabled"
